Like I mentioned in another thread, this was the first wizard ever that
I managed to keep alive until finding the quest portal.
I started the game on Sunday evening Finnish time and finished last night.

At start I had spellbooks of force bolt and magic missile. As soon as I
got enough Pw to cast magic missile, I didn't use force bolt much, mainly
for breaking statues.
And after getting my first orcish dagger, I don't think I ever wielded 
anything in combat but daggers and Magicbane. First the orcish dagger, then 
an elven one that I enchanted.

One lucky break was finding a spellbook of identify somewhere quite early
in the game (I didn't make notes about when). At first I cast it once every
time my Pw was at max, after taking off my metallic hat and iron shoes.
Mostly failed because the failure rate was still somewhere above 70, but
every now and then I managed to get something identified. So I wasn't 
surprised that divination was the first spell school that I got to
enhance my skills at. By the end of the game I had seen and identified
all potions, all rings except warning, and all scrolls except scare monster
and punishment.

I didn't find any altars before Sokoban, and the Minetown altar was 
cross-aligned, so I went quite far before doing any sacrificing.
Sokoban had the bag at the top, so I didn't have inventory management
or carrying capacity problems for a long time. 
I had already found two different kinds of gray stones before going to
the mines, one of which turned out to be a touchstone and the other one
a luckstone. But I cleared the mines anyway.

After finishing the mines I found the bones of my longest-living earlier
wizard on dungeon level 10, with a temple. The temple was cross-aligned 
like the one in the mines, and I don't attack peaceful priests (early in
the game it's too dangerous, and when I could survive that, I don't want 
to lose the intrinsic protection..) so still no sacrificing. The earlier
wizard had YASD'd by touching a cockatrice corpse. This was the first
co-aligned altar for him, and the first corpse he was going to sacrifice
was the cockatrice..
Anyway, I finally got an amulet of reflection from the corpse's inventory,
as well as a ring of free action. They were cursed, of course, but with
those two items I don't much care whether they are cursed or not, I wear
them anyway. So I did this time, too.
There were also some nice spellbooks in the sack he had dropped to stay
less burdened for carrying the corpses he was going to summon with his
wands. Not much other stuff that I used.

The next level was Bigroom (version 2, the one with dark square areas
North, South, West and East) and the Quest portal was also on the 
Bigroom level. I think I already had spell of identify at 0% failrate
by the time I was there, and that really helped a lot when I didn't
need to lug unwanted things around to be identified later instead of 
just picking up everything I liked and leaving the rest behind.

The only trouble was the lack of altars to sacrifice at. I had to go
as far down as dungeon level 19 to find an altar that didn't have a
cross-aligned priest guarding it. That altar was chaotic like me, and
there was no priest. Well, sacrifice monsters on one altar and donate
money on the other one. Still using up all my scrolls and wands of create
monster and sacrificing the hostiles didn't get me anything then.

So I went on further down the dungeon.
Medusa was on dungeon level 26, and the layout was the one where she is
in the middle of the level. Next to the stairs there was a trapdoor and
I fell through that to the next level, which was the Castle. I put on
my blindfold, climbed up the stairs and before I could lift my finger
towards Medusa, I had killed her. I guess she saw her reflection in my
amulet and decided she isn't supposed to live. By the door there was
another trapdoor, and I fell to the Castle level again and climbed back
again.

I walked around the Medusa island and found a spellbook of create monster.
Great. I read it and headed back to the only chaotic altar I had found.
Eventually I got the Magicbane and reached explevel 14. I had carried a
potion of gain level for a while, but preferred to get the exp by killing
monsters that might carry some interesting equipment.

Now I felt ready to try my first wizard quest. On Home 1 there was a 
gremlin that kept multiplying in the water, but all gremlins that I checked
were peaceful. By the time I reached the quest bottom, Dark One was 
apparently afraid of me. Instead of a fair fight, he escaped to the level 
above, but I reached the next stairs before him, so I could finish him
there. Since he was hostile to me, I thought it might be a good idea
to free his prisoners, and went back down to do it. Most of them were
peaceful to me, but some were ungrateful and I had to kill them.
When I had carried the Eye of Aethiopica for a while, I realized why
so many people have said that wizards get easier after the quest.
They really do, with the faster magic energy regeneration.

Back to the castle, and had no problem there. First I read a scroll of
teleportation in front of the moat and built a tunnel around the 
drawbridge so no eels can get to me while I stand there and no monsters
(except xorns) can get past me away from the Castle.
I played the bugle until I found the passtune, then started to cast
magic missiles through the door, occasionally checking there were no
interesting items on the drawbridge or in the portcullis, sometimes
closing the bridge and using the portcullis guillotine when there was
a disenchanter or somebody else that I didn't want to let come next to me.
I was still wearing a studded leather armor and there was no silver dragon
in the castle either. So I used the first charge of the Castle Wand 
(found at 0:3) for a silver dragon scale mail and later turned out to 
never use that wand again.

When Asmodeus had began his teleport away routine and I was chasing him,
somewhere during the battle he summoned Dispater. They escaped together
to the level above, which had been Baalzebub's level before I killed him.
One of them also summoned Geryon. I don't remember on which level I
killed each of them, but after they were all killed, I found myself on
the Baalz level near the downstairs surrounded by a yellow dragon, a
carnivorous ape, a minotaur, a master mind flayer and I don't remember
who else was there. One of the three named demons had summoned them.
I teleported the master mind flayer away, but to my disappointment it 
got only a few squares away and in a place that was not much more 
convenient to me, because it was between me and the stairs. Being bashed 
by all of them I was soon at about 30 Hp, the master mind flayer next to 
me and another mmf that I had telepathically sensed outside Baalz's house 
had come in and was getting close. And the carnivorous ape was holding me.

I looked at the wand of teleportation in my inventory and it had one
charge left. I broke the wand, clearing my escape route to the stairs.
I went downstairs to heal myself and think. Two master mind flayers
on the level above, and at least one of them close to the stairs.
I *hate* those bastards. 
I decided that getting my first wizard ascension is more important to me 
than keeping any conducts, so I used an uncursed scroll of genocide
for master mind flayers.
In good health and no more need to fight teleporting Asmodeus, Dispater
and Geryon, it was a lot easier to finish the rest of the crowd that
surrounded and nearly killed me just a few moves earlier.
Later, as a precaution, I used a blessed genocide on L (before seeing any 
arch-liches) and another uncursed one on the regular mind flayers.
Like I said, I *wanted* to ascend this guy.

When I had located the vibrating square and taken a trip to dlevel 1
and was coming back for Rodney, I blessed and quaffed the two potions of 
full healing that I had. I didn't even remember they were smoky. 
The first one released a djinni who gave me a wish (the second and last 
one I used).
I didn't feel like really missing anything, so I dug up some wishlist
and decided to ask for a blessed spellbook of finger of death.
Having studied it I saw it was at 100% failrate. Well, I had all my 
spell skills at basic level that time, having saved skill slots to be
used in a situation like this, when I see some spell at high failrate and
want to make it better. #enhancing attack spells to expert level got it
to 0% fail. Yes, I really had enough skill slots saved, and really had
practiced enough to go straight from basic to expert.

In Sanctum, when I was entering the big hall around the temple, there was
a cockatrice next to the door. I wielded its corpse most of the way to
the temple and back. Then, on the last square before returning to the
graveyard, there was a pit and I was burdened.. luckily I had replaced
the amulet of reflection with an amulet of life saving somewhere earlier
after putting on the SDSM. I dropped a great deal of stuff in the
Sanctum level to get unburdened, and in the Valley I noticed I was
burdened again.. my bag of holding was still blessed, so that didn't
make me burdened. But I didn't remember what I had picked up to burden
me, and I ended up dropping even the invocation items to the Medusa level.

The mysterious force slowed me totally 12 times, but I don't complain
about that after sometimes struggling against it a lot more:
41->41,39->40,40->40,39->39,38->38,36->37,37->38,34->35 (this time
the wizard also came back for the first time),34->34,34->34,34->35,32->33.
The stairs to Vlad's tower were on level 39, I guess the game tried to make
me go there again. 38 was the Orcus level. I didn't notice anything special
on level 34 that the game wanted to make me go through again and again..

The Wizard came back 5 times: in Gehennom level 35 like I mentioned, 
DoD levels 22, 18 and 13 and finally on Earth. 
"So thou thought thou couldst kill me, fool."
Yeah, I said each time, putting down the Amulet (to reduce its effects on
spellcasting) and gave him the finger.
No double troubling, no stealing stuff from me. Just finger of death each
time and he believed it for a while.

On dungeon level 18, after showing finger to the Wizard, I bumped into
a nymph who took my Magicbane. Verry annoying. I kept on chasing the nymph
around the level, occasionally dropping the Amulet to finger creatures
that were on my way but mostly just walking around them. What a nasty 
little teleporting bitch! Well, finally I managed to show my finger to
her and got Magicbane back.

On the planes, I used scrolls of gold detection to find the portals, as
usual. One of them was cursed and the others were uncursed. I used the
cursed one on Earth.
On Astral, I arrived a bit left of the center, so I started checking the
altars from left. 
The leftmost altar was guarded by Famine and cross-aligned.
Somewhere in the South corridor, coming to the middle altar, I found
myself with Hp 4. The lowest figure since a long time. I prayed to
Anhur and he healed me as I expected.
The altar in the middle was the right one, guarded by Pestilence.

When I found out I was on the right altar, I removed the amulet of life
saving that I had worn until using up the previous one in the Sanctum.
I didn't want Anhur to see me wearing it when giving Anhur the other Amulet.
I had two scrolls of taming in my bag and had an idea about getting some 
pets at the end to follow me to the Demigod bar, but there was only 
an insect or two in the temple when I got there. And the guardian angel
of Anhur was coming in, surprising me by still being alive and so near.
So I decided not to take other pets after all.

